# CITATION.cff — Citation File Format 1.2.0 (D-28).
#
# This file is metadata about the repository, not a release announcement. There
# is no release, no tag and no demo, and there will not be one until the
# evidence gate of GOVERNANCE.md §8 is satisfied (D-12). Three fields therefore
# need reading carefully:
#
#   * `version: 0.0.0` tracks the maturity badge in README.md, which currently
#     reads `status: design`. It is not a released version number.
#   * `date-released` records the date this public design artifact was made
#     available, which is what CFF's field means. It is not the date of a
#     software release, because none exists.
#   * `license` is Apache-2.0 because CFF has exactly one licence field and the
#     code licence is the one a citing tool will act on. The repository is
#     dual-licensed; the abstract says so and `REUSE.toml` is authoritative.
#
# The abstract's expansion and status line are the D-24 wording, and must match
# README.md character for character; `epppsynth/tests/test_rights.py` checks it.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you refer to this project, please cite it using the metadata in this file,
  and please cite the status line with it: this is a design and planning
  artifact, it has not been validated, and it is not for clinical use.
title: "epppsynth"
type: software
version: "0.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-23"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/willtfarrington/epppsynth"
authors:
  - given-names: "W. Taylor"
    family-names: "Farrington"
    email: "william.t.farrington@gmail.com"
abstract: >-
  epppsynth — existential perspectives for physicians & patients. Design and
  planning artifact — v1 in progress; no release, no demo, no validation. It is
  the design for a local, offline-capable reflection aid: given a few
  explicitly supplied, structured facts about a manifestly fictional clinical
  encounter and a stated purpose, it is intended to produce three to five
  concise, revisable waypoints. It is not therapy, not clinical decision
  support, not a risk detector, and not a source of clinical recommendations.
  It is built for its author's private local use; the repository is public as a
  source and portfolio artifact, and public source availability is not evidence
  of efficacy, safety, approval, or suitability. Licensing is split and this
  file can carry only one licence field: the licence recorded above is
  Apache-2.0, which covers the code, while the content model, the concept
  registry, the documentation and the roadmap are licensed CC BY 4.0 — the
  boundary is in REUSE.toml and NOTICE. Review is author-only: no clinician,
  educator, ethicist, patient, person with lived experience of serious illness,
  or accessibility reviewer has reviewed this project. The conceptual sources
  it cites are read as input and never redistributed; what each one permits is
  recorded in epppsynth/docs/rights.md. Work in progress; not validated; not
  for clinical use.
references:
  # The four content traditions of D-14, so that anyone citing this software is
  # pointed at the primary sources rather than at this project's paraphrase of
  # them. Two of the four are literature families rather than single works;
  # they are recorded as such rather than being collapsed onto one convenient
  # citation. Every one of them, with its rights record, is in
  # epppsynth/docs/rights.md.
  - type: book
    title: "Existential Psychotherapy"
    authors:
      - given-names: "Irvin D."
        family-names: "Yalom"
    year: 1980
    publisher:
      name: "Basic Books"
    isbn: "978-0-465-02147-5"
    notes: >-
      The source of the four givens, which this project labels as one tradition
      among several and never as a general model. Read as input from a copy the
      author owns; not redistributed, and no derived text is published.
  - type: report
    title: >-
      SAMHSA's Concept of Trauma and Guidance for a Trauma-Informed Approach
    authors:
      - name: "Substance Abuse and Mental Health Services Administration (US)"
    year: 2014
    notes: >-
      Reuse terms UNVERIFIED — held at reference-only-pending-rights-check
      until cleared (D-62). Referenced, not ingested.
  - type: generic
    title: >-
      Serious-illness communication evidence — a literature family, not a
      single work
    authors:
      - name: >-
          Multiple authors; the family is recorded under source_id
          serious-illness-communication-literature in
          epppsynth/docs/rights.md
    notes: >-
      The closest evidence analogues to this project are null-to-adverse, and
      GOVERNANCE.md §11 records what that means for every public claim made
      here.
  - type: generic
    title: "The moral-injury literature — a literature family, not a single work"
    authors:
      - name: >-
          Multiple authors; the family is recorded under source_id
          moral-injury-literature in epppsynth/docs/rights.md
    notes: >-
      Definitionally contested. The project's charter clause is that moral
      injury arises from conditions, not individual deficiency.
